 "captions": [
  {
   "t": "Here's a math trick banks don't teach you. It tells you how fast your money doubles… in two seconds.",
   "s": 0.05,
   "e": 4.73
  },
  {
   "t": "Take seventy-two. Divide it by your yearly return. That's how many years it takes to double your money.",
   "s": 4.93,
   "e": 9.84
  },
  {
   "t": "At eight percent a year, seventy-two divided by eight is nine. Your money doubles in about nine years.",
   "s": 10.04,
   "e": 15.18
  },
  {
   "t": "At four percent, it takes eighteen years. At twelve percent, just six.",
   "s": 15.38,
   "e": 19.69
  },
  {
   "t": "But it works backwards too. A credit card at twenty-two percent doubles your debt in about three years.",
   "s": 19.89,
   "e": 24.61
  },
  {
